.TH FL-MEDIA-PLAYER 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.4" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-media-player \- video and music player (formerly fl-video)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-media-player\fR [\fB\-\-fullscreen\fR] [\fB\-\-software\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIURL\fR|\fIPLAYLIST\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Plays video and audio files, playlists and network streams with \fBGStreamer\fR: the formats and
codecs it can play depend on the GStreamer plugins installed (the "good", "bad" and "libav"
plugin sets cover nearly everything; a missing plugin is named in the error message). Several
files make a playlist; files dropped on the window are added to it (with Ctrl
held, they replace it). Web addresses that \fByt-dlp\fR understands (YouTube and many other sites) also
play: the player keeps its own yt-dlp and the QuickJS-ng JavaScript engine in
\fI~/.local/share/fldesktop/media-player/bin\fR, downloaded from their GitHub
releases, checked against the published SHA-256 sums and updated once a day
(distribution packages of yt-dlp are usually too old for the sites). This
needs Python 3.10 or newer and curl; \fBWeb Videos\fR in the menu turns it off,
and then an installed \fByt-dlp\fR is used.
Subtitle files next to a video (same name) are loaded automatically.
.PP
The playlist sidebar (\fBL\fR, or the list button) shows the playlist: double-click or Enter
plays an entry, Delete removes it, the buttons below add files, move entries up and down, turn
shuffle on and off, cycle repeat (off, the whole playlist, one entry) and save the playlist.
M3U, M3U8 and PLS playlist files open like media files and are saved in either format.
.PP
Music shows its cover art: embedded in the file, or \fIcover.jpg\fR, \fIfolder.jpg\fR and the
like next to it. The title, artist and album come from the file's tags. Other programs, the
panel's now playing row and the media keys control the player through MPRIS
(\fIorg.mpris.MediaPlayer2.fl_media_player\fR); while music plays, logind does not suspend the
computer for being idle.
.PP
\fBfl-video\fR is a link to \fBfl-media-player\fR, for scripts and file associations that use
the old name.
.PP
The position in each file is remembered when you quit and playback resumes there next time
(\fBResume Where I Left Off\fR in the menu turns this off). The screen stays on while a video plays.
.PP
Video is drawn with OpenGL; without a usable OpenGL driver it falls back to software
rendering (GStreamer scales the picture to the window).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fullscreen\fR
Start in full screen.
.TP
\fB\-\-software\fR
Use the software renderer (also \fBFLD_VIDEO_SW=1\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-warm\-registry\fR
Let GStreamer build its plugin registry and exit. The session runs this
once after login (\fI/etc/xdg/autostart/fl-media-player-warmup.desktop\fR),
so that the first start after an install or update is not slow. On machines
with less than 2 GB of memory it does nothing. The player itself starts
GStreamer only when the first file is played.
.SH KEYS
.TP
\fBSpace\fR, \fBK\fR, click
Play / pause.
.TP
\fBLeft\fR / \fBRight\fR
Seek 5 seconds (with \fBShift\fR: 1 minute). \fB,\fR / \fB.\fR step one frame.
.TP
\fBUp\fR / \fBDown\fR, mouse wheel
Volume. \fBM\fR mutes.
.TP
\fBF\fR, \fBF11\fR, double-click
Full screen; \fBEscape\fR leaves it.
.TP
\fB[\fR / \fB]\fR, \fBBackspace\fR
Slower / faster, normal speed.
.TP
\fBN\fR / \fBP\fR
Next / previous playlist entry.
.TP
\fBL\fR
Show or hide the playlist.
.TP
\fBJ\fR, \fBV\fR, \fB#\fR
Next subtitle track, show/hide subtitles, next audio track.
.TP
\fBS\fR
Screenshot into the Pictures folder.
.TP
\fBI\fR
Show file and codec information.
.TP
\fBCtrl+O\fR, \fBCtrl+U\fR, \fBCtrl+R\fR, \fBCtrl+Q\fR
Open files, open an address, repeat (off, all, one), quit.
.PP
Right-click (or the menu button) for audio, video and subtitle track selection, loading subtitle
files, speed, the playlist and the other options.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/media-player.ini\fR
Volume, the resume setting, the playlist sidebar, shuffle and repeat (read from
\fIvideo.ini\fR the first time).
.TP
\fI~/.cache/fldesktop/video-positions.ini\fR
Remembered positions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBFLD_VIDEO_SW\fR
Set to 1 to always use the software renderer.
.TP
\fBFLD_VIDEO_DEBUG\fR
Print renderer messages, GStreamer warnings and error details.
.SH SOUND AND CHAPTERS
The right-click menu's \fBAudio\fR submenu turns volume levelling on and off (from ReplayGain tags,
starting with the next track; on by default) and opens a 10-band \fBEqualizer\fR with presets
(Flat, Bass, Treble, Voice, Loudness); it is heard at once and kept for the next start.
Files with chapters (Matroska, MP4, Ogg) get a \fBChapters\fR submenu that jumps to one.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgst-launch-1.0\fR(1), \fByt-dlp\fR(1), \fBfl-files\fR(1)
